# Sprout backend - manual smoke requests (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP).
# Run register, copy the login token into @token, then call the protected route.

@base = http://localhost:4000

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Register a merchant (defaults to onboarding / pending - never active)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "business_name": "Demo Store",
  "owner_name": "Ada Demo",
  "phone": "08031234567",
  "email": "ada@sprout.test",
  "password": "sprout-demo-1234"
}

### Login (returns { token, merchant })
# @name login
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@sprout.test",
  "password": "sprout-demo-1234"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Protected route - with valid token
GET {{base}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Protected route - no token (expect 401)
GET {{base}}/api/me

### Verify identity (mock mode) - verifies + creates sub-account + activates
# Any 11-digit id NOT ending in 0000 passes in mock mode.
POST {{base}}/api/verification
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id_type": "BVN",
  "id_number": "22212345678"
}

### Verify identity - failure path (mock: id ending in 0000 fails)
POST {{base}}/api/verification
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id_type": "NIN",
  "id_number": "22212340000"
}

### Create a Dynamic Invoice (merchant must be verified/active)
# @name invoice
POST {{base}}/api/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_name": "Chidi Buyer",
  "description": "Order #42",
  "amount": 15000,
  "due_date": "2026-12-31"
}

### List my invoices
GET {{base}}/api/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get one invoice + its payment/settlement
GET {{base}}/api/invoices/{{invoice.response.body.invoice.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Connect an existing Monnify account (read-only; creds validated then encrypted)
# Mock mode: any creds work unless api_key ends in "BAD" (deterministic failure).
# @name connected
POST {{base}}/api/connected-accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "business_name": "External Shop",
  "api_key": "MK_TEST_EXTERNAL",
  "secret_key": "SK_TEST_EXTERNAL",
  "contract_code": "1234567"
}

### List connected accounts (never returns credentials)
GET {{base}}/api/connected-accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sync a connected account's transaction history (idempotent)
POST {{base}}/api/connected-accounts/{{connected.response.body.account.id}}/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Analytics - my own merchant data
GET {{base}}/api/analytics?days=30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Analytics - a connected account (same response shape)
GET {{base}}/api/analytics?connected_account_id={{connected.response.body.account.id}}&days=30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Monnify collection webhook (no auth; HMAC-SHA512 of the RAW body in the
### monnify-signature header, keyed by MONNIFY_WEBHOOK_SECRET). The signature
### can't be hardcoded here - `npm run smoke` exercises this end to end.
POST {{base}}/api/webhooks/monnify
Content-Type: application/json
monnify-signature: <hex hmac-sha512 of the body>

{
  "eventType": "SUCCESSFUL_TRANSACTION",
  "eventData": {
    "transactionReference": "<from invoice response>",
    "paymentReference": "PAYREF-001",
    "paymentStatus": "PAID",
    "product": { "reference": "<invoice_reference>" }
  }
}
